# CHANGELOG

One short sentence per change, saying what it does. Nothing else: no detail, no reasoning, no what
it was like before. Those belong in the code and its comments, where whoever needs them is already
standing.

Good:

```
a project now waits for the start button on the board before any of its tasks is worked.
```

Bad, and this is the whole of one entry saying what the line above says:

```
a project now waits for you to start it. an agent that had just laid a plan out with you would go
straight on to handing its tasks to subagents, and there was nothing between talking a project over
and having it worked apart: the only way to stop it was to be quicker than it. an open row on the
board has a start button now, and until it is pressed nothing of that project moves.
```
